// Components: functional blocks on the one 1 m grid. Every stat is the block's own, nothing is
// scaled at load. Devices that tier up are ladders, one entry per rung ("thruster-t1".."-t5"),
// sized and weighted from docs/grid-figures.md (Empyrion's proportions, counted in 1 m cells).
// Units, one constant per quantity, anchored so today's small part x 8 is about the bottom rung:
//   hp         hit points (a plated iron cube is 158)
//   mass       tonnes (the figures' kg / 1000)
//   power      MW: positive generates, negative is drawn at full load; the figures' kW x 0.0005
//   thrust     kN, pushing the structure forward (-Z) out of the exhaust at +Z; the figures' index x 0.5
//   fuel       units held; the figures' kWh x 0.5
//   storage    SU added to the one shared storage of the structure (the figures' SU as is)
//   function   core, chair, thruster, generator, fuel, container, door, light, turret, ladder or
//              stairs (two 0.5 m steps rising toward +z, the slope's way: a shape is one convex
//              hull, so the steps are parts and collide as they are)
//   size       cells [x, y, z] (default one); parts boxes span -0.5..0.5 over the whole size.
//              A thruster's exhaust axis is z, so its long side (the figures' height) is z here
//   group      a variant family placed from one item, the size picked like a shape (doors)
//   seat, eye  chairs: where a seated person's hips rest and where their eyes are, in the
//              block's -0.5..0.5 box
//   was        old ids this block replaces, so old blueprints still load
//   attach     faces other blocks can attach to ("all", "none" or a list such as ["-y"])
//   airtight   faces that seal air (doors: airtightOpen applies while open)
//   covers     faces that may hide the cell face behind them (for culling). Only ever a limit:
//              a face hides nothing unless an opaque part really covers the whole of it
//   collide    cell, parts (the part boxes) or none
//   parts      boxes or cylinders in box units; style body (takes paint), dark, accent, glow,
//              glass; closedOnly parts belong to a door leaf. A part may also set its finish:
//              color, accent, pattern (a paint pattern, fine-hazard or grille), texture, metal,
//              symbol (shown on a glow part, stencilled on anything else), anim and speed (a glow
//              that pulses or blinks). Bolts, vents, screens and trim come from DeviceDetail.cs,
//              one rule per function, not from here
